    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\r\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\r\n    <span class=\"time\">30 min</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip company\">Flipkart</span><span class=\"chip company\">Razorpay</span>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <h1>API &amp; Interface Design for LLD</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">Your classes are drawn. Now the interviewer asks \"what does the outside world call?\" This page teaches you to design the public surface of the orchestrator class: method names that say what the user wants, request and response types, an error contract you can explain, validation in the right place, idempotent operations that survive retries, and a clean driver for machine-coding rounds.</p>\r\n"
